WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.430
At Slop University, Dr Mirela Hanke is Deputy Convenor of the Living Dashboard.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.650
I study how a dashboard shapes the choices it's only meant to inform.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.890
A number starts out as a measurement.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.130
Then people start deciding by it.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.780
And then, quietly, it becomes the goal.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.774
A cafe chain that measures friendliness by its tip screen.

00:00:23.074 --> 00:00:27.300
New vending machines, credited with a point the day they went in.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.090
Gym members who cancel just in time to keep their score clean.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.900
No postdoc at Slop University has a higher h-index.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.120
Eleven hundred and fifty-eight citations.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.930
And an h-index of twenty-eight.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.380
When everyone is chasing a number,

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.800
I ask what it was for.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.220
Find more on our website,

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.440
follow us on Bluesky,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:50.590
or drop us an email.
